      "body": "The AMD test suite was running a special comparison mode that copies an NVIDIA-specific GPU instruction sequence. PyTorch exposes AMD GPUs through the same `torch.cuda` API, so the old device check did not skip those tests on ROCm.\n\nOn MI300, the AMD compiler reports `could not allocate output register for constraint 'f'`, and the comparison returns the wrong result.\n\nThis change:\n\n- stops `match_cutedsl_decode` with a clear error before it reaches the GPU on ROCm;\n- skips only the two NVIDIA instruction-parity tests on ROCm;\n- keeps the normal KDA recurrence test running on ROCm;\n- adds a ROCm regression test for the clear error.\n\nNo production caller currently enables `match_cutedsl_decode`, so this does not change AMD serving behavior.\n\nRelated: #43991 addresses a separate KDA Q/K normalization mismatch.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `python -m compileall` on both changed files\n- repository Ruff lint selection\n- Ruff formatting check\n- isort check\n- GPU coverage left to draft PR CI\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38382153199](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38382153199)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38382153055](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38382153055)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38382153467](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38382153467)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
